📌 What is StandardCopyOption.REPLACE_EXISTING?
When using Files.copy(...), Java needs to know:“What should I do if the file already exists at the destination?”
That’s where StandardCopyOption.REPLACE_EXISTING comes in.
➡️ If the file already exists at targetPath, Java will throw:FileAlreadyExistsException
🛡️ With REPLACE_EXISTING: Files.copy(inputStream, targetPath, StandardCopyOption.REPLACE_EXISTING);
➡️ It silently overwrites the existing file with the new one.

💡 When to use?

| Scenario                            | Use `REPLACE_EXISTING`? | Why                                                          |
| ----------------------------------- | ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |
| Always want latest image uploaded   | ✅ Yes                   | New image should replace the old one                         |
| Want to keep all uploads unique     | ❌ No                    | Better to create unique file names (like using UUID in name) |
| Accidentally reusing same file name | ✅ Safe                  | Prevents `FileAlreadyExistsException`                        |


